  "Question": "The year \\(2002\\) is a palindrome (a number that reads the same from left to right as it does from right to left). What is the product of the digits of the next year after \\(2002\\) that is a palindrome?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(0\\)",
    "B": "\\(4\\)",
    "C": "\\(9\\)",
    "D": "\\(16\\)",
    "E": "\\(25\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "A four-digit palindrome is determined by its first two digits: the last two must be those digits in reverse order. Keeping the first two digits \\(20\\) gives only \\(2002\\). The next possible first two digits are \\(21\\), which give \\(2112\\). Any larger first two digits produce a larger year, so \\(2112\\) is the next palindrome.\n\nIts digit product is\n\\[\n2\\cdot1\\cdot1\\cdot2=4.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{4}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
